  "title": "National Minimum Wage and National Living Wage rates - GOV.UK",
  "content": [
    {
      "p": "The hourly rate for the minimum wage depends on your age and whether you’re an apprentice ."
    },
    {
      "p": "This page is also available in Welsh (Cymraeg) ."
    },
    {
      "p": "You must be at least:"
    },
    {
      "li": "school leaving age to get the National Minimum Wage"
    },
    {
      "li": "aged 21 to get the National Living Wage - the minimum wage will still apply for workers aged 20 and under"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Current rates"
    },
    {
      "p": "The rates change on 1 April every year."
    },
    {
      "table": [
        ["", "21 and over", "18 to 20", "Under 18", "Apprentice"],
        ["April 2026", "£12.71", "£10.85", "£8", "£8"],
        ["April 2027", "£13.21", "£11.27", "£8.31", "£8.31"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "h3": "Apprentices"
    },
    {
      "p": "Apprentices are entitled to the apprentice rate if they’re either:"
    },
    {
      "li": "aged under 19"
    },
    {
      "li": "aged 19 or over and in the first year of their apprenticeship"
    },
    {
      "p": "Example"
    },
    {
      "p": "An apprentice aged 21 in the first year of their apprenticeship is entitled to a minimum hourly rate of £8."
    },
    {
      "p": "Apprentices are entitled to the minimum wage for their age if they both:"
    },
    {
      "li": "are aged 19 or over"
    },
    {
      "li": "have completed the first year of their apprenticeship"
    },
    {
      "p": "Example"
    },
    {
      "p": "An apprentice aged 21 who has completed the first year of their apprenticeship is entitled to a minimum hourly rate of £12.71."
    },
    {
      "h2": "Previous rates"
    },
    {
      "p": "The following rates were for the National Living Wage and the National Minimum Wage from April 2019."
    },
    {
      "h3": "Rates between 1 April 2024 and 31 March 2026"
    },
    {
      "p": "Since 1 April 2024 the National Living Wage has been for those aged 21 and over."
    },
    {
      "table": [
        ["", "21 and over", "18 to 20", "Under 18", "Apprentice"],
        ["April 2025 to March 2026", "£12.21", "£10", "£7.55", "£7.55"],
        ["April 2024 to March 2025", "£11.44", "£8.60", "£6.40", "£6.40"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "h3": "Rates between 1 April 2021 and 31 March 2024"
    },
    {
      "p": "Between 1 April 2021 and 31 March 2024 the National Living Wage was for those aged 23 and over."
    },
    {
      "table": [
        ["", "23 and over", "21 to 22", "18 to 20", "Under 18", "Apprentice"],
        ["April 2023 to March 2024", "£10.42", "£10.18", "£7.49", "£5.28", "£5.28"],
        ["April 2022 to March 2023", "£9.50", "£9.18", "£6.83", "£4.81", "£4.81"],
        ["April 2021 to March 2022", "£8.91", "£8.36", "£6.56", "£4.62", "£4.30"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "h3": "Rates before 1 April 2021"
    },
    {
      "p": "Before 1 April 2021 the National Living Wage was for those aged 25 and over."
    },
    {
      "table": [
        ["", "25 and over", "21 to 24", "18 to 20", "Under 18", "Apprentice"],
        ["April 2020 to March 2021", "£8.72", "£8.20", "£6.45", "£4.55", "£4.15"],
        ["April 2019 to March 2020", "£8.21", "£7.70", "£6.15", "£4.35", "£3.90"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "h2": "Who gets the minimum wage"
    },
    {
      "p": "Read the information on who is entitled to the minimum wage ."
    },
    {
      "p": "You can use the minimum wage calculator to check whether the National Minimum Wage or National Living Wage is being paid."
    },
    {
      "p": "Contact Acas if you’re not getting the National Minimum Wage and think you should be."
    }
  ],
